Chase H.Q. for RISC OS
======================

This is a 32-bit RISC OS build of the reconstructed ZX Spectrum Chase H.Q.
game. It supports one game at a time and defaults to the 128K version.

Starting and stopping
---------------------

Select the iconbar icon to open the game window and start playing. Closing
the window stops the current game but leaves Chase H.Q. on the iconbar. Use
Quit from the iconbar menu, or Ctrl-Q, to close the whole application.

The iconbar menu can start a new 48K or 128K game, pause, restart, choose an
integer window scale, enter fullscreen mode, show program information, or
quit. Info is the first item and Quit is the last.

Controls
--------

The original Spectrum keyboard is available while the game window has the
input caret. Select inside the game window to give it the caret. The original
default driving keys are:

    K / L           steer left / right
    A / Z           accelerate / brake
    N               change gear
    Space           turbo boost

The arrow keys emulate a Kempston joystick. Keypad Enter is its fire button.
The game can redefine its own Spectrum keys in the usual way.

Host shortcuts
--------------

    F2              new 128K game
    F3              new 48K game
    F5              pause or resume
    F6              restart
    F7 to F10       window scale 1x to 4x
    F11             enter fullscreen mode
    Escape          leave fullscreen mode
    Ctrl-Q          quit the application

Fullscreen mode
---------------

Fullscreen play selects the closest suitable 4-bpp screen mode and centres
the game at the largest whole-pixel scale that fits. To override the choice,
set ChaseHQ$ScreenMode to a RISC OS mode number or mode string before running
the application, for example:

    *Set ChaseHQ$ScreenMode X800 Y600 C16

Escape returns to the saved desktop mode. Fullscreen play is deliberately
single-tasking: other applications are not given time and other host
shortcuts are not serviced until Chase H.Q. returns to its window. A game
paused before entering fullscreen remains visible while paused.

Requirements and limitations
----------------------------

Chase H.Q. requires a 32-bit RISC OS system with the Wimp, ColourTrans and
SpriteExtend. It does not support 26-bit or 64-bit systems. This first native
release is intentionally silent; AY and beeper audio are deferred. Save
games, networking, CRT effects and multiple simultaneous games are also not
provided by this release.
